{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You shall not take up.</b> In an oath of imprecation — as in וְנָשָׂא בוֹ אָלָה לְהַאֲלֹתוֹ (1 Kings 8:31)." "<b>In vain.</b> For a lie, for there is no doubt that the imprecation of the oath takes effect upon the swearer in such a case." "<b>For YHWH will not clear the one who takes up His name in vain.</b> For futility and without need — for even if one swears to the truth, YHWH will not clear him from the imprecation of the oath; how much more so when one swears to a lie. For it is not to His honor that a person take up His name, except to establish some truth that cannot be established without it. But an oath in His name when it is for a lie — when the swearer says 'this is true,' just as the blessed El is true — behold, he denies and profanes His name, as though saying that the blessed El is not true, as it says: וְלֹא תִשָּׁבְעוּ בִשְׁמִי לַשֶּׁקֶר, וְחִלַּלְתָּ אֶת שֵׁם אֱלֹהֶיךָ (Leviticus 19:12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:31.700960976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}